logy Group Assessment; <sc>fact</sc>-<sc>g</sc> = Functional Assessment of Cancer Therapy&#x02014;General scale; <sc>fact</sc>-<sc>br</sc> = Functional Assessment of Cancer Therapy&#x02014;Brain subscale; <sc>eortc bcm</sc> 20 = European Organization for Research and Treatment of Cancer Brain Cancer Module; <sc>mmse</sc> = Mini Mental Status Examination; <sc>kps</sc> = Karnofsky performance status; <sc>esas</sc> = Edmonton Symptom Assessment Scale; <sc>eortc qlq</sc>-30 = European Organization for Research and Treatment of Cancer Core Quality of Life Questionnaire; <sc>hvlt</sc> = Hopkins Verbal Learning Test; <sc>cowa</sc> = Controlled Oral Word Association; <sc>wbrt</sc> = whole-brain radiotherapy; <sc>poms</sc>-<sc>sf</sc> = Profile of Mood States&#x02013;Short Form; <sc>mmsi</sc> = Mini Mental State Inventory; <sc>ns</sc> = nonsignificant.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="tVIII-co15-5-226e25" position="float"><label>TABLE VIII</label><caption><p>Studies focused on managing brain metastases through corticosteroids</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Reference</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Study arms</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Patients (n)</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Median survival</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Overall response rate (<sc>cr</sc>+<sc>pr</sc>)</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><sc>qol</sc> assessment</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Tools Neurologic function or symptom control</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Other assessment</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><sc>qol</sc> instruments (n)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Horton <italic>et al.,</italic> 1971 <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b40-co15-5-226e25">40</xref></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Oral prednisone and <sc>wbrt</sc></td><td align="